The first-stage C++ SSH service fetches these pinned source dependencies at
configure time:

- libssh2 1.11.1 — BSD 3-Clause license; https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2
- nlohmann/json 3.11.3 — MIT license; https://github.com/nlohmann/json
- cpp-httplib 0.18.3 — MIT license; https://github.com/yhirose/cpp-httplib
- OpenSSL 3.5.9 — Apache License 2.0; https://www.openssl.org/source/

The OpenSSL license text is packaged beside the C++ SSH service as
`$RESOURCE/ssh-service/OPENSSL-LICENSE.txt`.

The packaged desktop application does not bundle a JavaScript runtime. The
desktop host is C++ and the Agent is Python, so no Node.js runtime is downloaded,
staged or referenced during the package build. `scripts/node-runtime.json` no
longer exists and no `$RESOURCE/runtime` directory is produced; an earlier
version of this notice described a Node runtime that the packaging pipeline has
since dropped.

The packaged Python Agent includes third-party Python distributions. Their license
metadata and available license texts are collected into
`$RESOURCE/python-agent/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt` during the package build.
